SWEET AOC start + service discovery (patch 0165, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A8), boot-arg sweetaoc=3 (1 = A4 reads, 2 = A6 load).
sweetaoc=3 runs the A6 load of patch 0164 unchanged; after "gsa load ok", in the same thread (bsd/dev/sweet_aoc_start.c, pure logic
bsd/dev/sweet_aoc_start.h, host test shim/aoc_start_host_test.c, cites docs/research/50 s.6 and the stock DT/source): chipid read
(GS101, rev 0x11 as stock), aoc_req/SysMMU read, the parameter block of aoc_pass_fw_information at carveout + image_size (22
entries; board id 0x20302, rev 0x10000 from the stock DT aoc-board-cfg "o6"), the SSMT bypass of aoc_configure_ssmt (64 writes,
restored on every stop where the AOC was not started), then over the patch 0162 transport hwmgr.aoc GET_STATE, START (only after
a LOADED reply; gate in bsd/dev/sweet_tipc.h, which gains an optional sub sequence; sweettrusty=2 unchanged), GET_STATE; poll the
control block magic 0xA0C00A0C <= 5 s; read the service table (read only), aoc_req := 0 as aoc_did_become_online. No SysMMU or
S2MPU write, no mailbox write, no AOC reset, no audio path, no amp. Lines: "SWEET AOC: online services=N ..." + one line per
service, or "SWEET AOC: start stop <why>" with a read-only dump of the AOC mailbox, aoc_req and the SysMMU. No retry.

